From c0ca2b2922db54ed6cff5d8ae009de755a77cc69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:23:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): rebuild boards with table b-tree damage in
 place, reconcile sync, keep forensic copies [daveey]

hermes kanban recover (and the gateway dispatcher, automatically, when it pauses a damaged
board) salvages a board REINDEX cannot fix: out of process, under a per-board recovery lock,
from a backup-API snapshot; every table read forward, backward, through each index and by
point lookup; missing rows filled from the newest healthy quarantine; per-table loss report;
written back INTO the live file with the backup API so open connections stay valid; follow-up
card; sync reconcile. Replaces the manual dump/load + mv that raced three times on the hub
(2026-10-28) and corrupted the copies it installed.

- kanban sync reconcile: upload rows the service lacks (lost outbox), restore own rows the
  file lost from the service snapshot, never overwrite rows still present.
- Quarantine rotation only prunes content-addressed copies; a burst no longer deletes
  manual forensic copies.
- conftest drops HERMES_KANBAN_* before collection, not only per test.
